    <content type="html" xml:base="https://pratik.deoghare.com/barkdown/posts/welcome/">&lt;p&gt;This is the first post of a site made with barkdown. Posts are written in brashtag: plain text, with&#xA;&lt;code&gt;#tag{...}&lt;/code&gt; bags where structure is needed.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Write a paragraph, leave a blank line, write the next one. That is most of it.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Everything above the &lt;code&gt;#more{}&lt;/code&gt; marker is the excerpt shown on the home page. The rest appears only on the&#xA;post&amp;#39;s own page.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;next-steps&#34;&gt;Next steps &lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#next-steps&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Run &lt;code&gt;barkdown serve&lt;/code&gt; and open the address it prints.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Edit this file and watch the browser reload.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Read &lt;a href=&#34;/barkdown/posts/tour/&#34;&gt;A tour of barkdown&lt;/a&gt; for every tag barkdown understands.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Run &lt;code&gt;barkdown build&lt;/code&gt; and copy &lt;code&gt;public/&lt;/code&gt; to any static host.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;</content>
  </entry>
